6922517	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Differently &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;Friedrich J. − Kammenhuber A. 2012b&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;, p. 565-566 s.v. &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ḫe/inkan:&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ke&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_corr&gt;!&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_corr&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;dan&lt;del_in/&gt;i&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; (Text: &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;kuedani&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;). The sign, however, looks like &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;AŠ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt; and not a broken &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;NI&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;. &lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922518	For the restoration of the verb &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;ari&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; &quot;it arrives&quot; with &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;annaš&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; UD-&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;aš&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; (&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;šiwaz&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;) as subject cf. the similar phrase in the treaty of Muwattalli II with Alakšandu of Wiluša CTH 76 KUB 21.1 i 64 &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;&lt;del_in/&gt;A-N&lt;del_fin/&gt;A&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;M&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;alakšandu&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;laes_in/&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;ŠA&lt;laes_fin/&gt;&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;AMA-&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;KA&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;UD&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-az&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ari&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; “&lt;del_in/&gt;But when&lt;del_fin/&gt; for (you), Alakšandu, the day of your mother arrives”. A remarkable feature is the left-dislocation of the ablative phrase &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;IŠ-TU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Numeral&gt;10&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Numeral&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;LÚ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;MEŠ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Numeral&gt;20&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Numeral&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;LÚ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;MEŠ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt; and its resumption by the relative pronoun in the dat.-loc. pl. &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;kuedas&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;. On the phenomenon of left-dislocation see &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;Hoffner H.A. − Melchert H.C. 2008a&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;, 408f.
6922519	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Or &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;NÍG&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-aš-za&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;. Both the reading and the meaning of the term remain unclear. Cf. also obv. I 24.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922520	Restoration based on KBo 41.163 l. col. 1′: &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;&lt;del_fin/&gt;x&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;BAL&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-kán&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;ŠÀ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;MU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-ti&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ta-ra-an-za&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &quot; and KBo 44.222 obv. 6′: &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;nu-kán&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;BE&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-an&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;ŠÀ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;MU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-ti-ma&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ta-ra-x&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;&lt;del_in/&gt;).
6922521	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Restoration based on obv. I 7; obv. I 22; obv. II 44.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922522	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;The vertical wedge of &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;MA&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt; is missing. For the reading &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;nam-ma-ma&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; see obv. II 24 and 36.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922523	 <P_f_Footnote>A vertical wedge of the erased sign is still visible. Possibly, the scribe first intended to write <SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN>MA</SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN> or <SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN>TA</SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN>.</P_f_Footnote>
6922524	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;The horizontal wedge was erroneously erased by the scribe.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922525	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Possibly the horizontal wedge, rendered here as &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;AŠ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;, was part of a more complex sign that was erroneously written and afterwards partly erased.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922526	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Since, according to obv. II 5-12, the anger of only one deity of Ḫattuša is ascertained, the plural determinative &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;MEŠ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt; is probably erroneous.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922527	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Judging from his translation, &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;Beal R.H. 1997a&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;, 210 apparently restores &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ḫu-eš-wa-an-za&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; after &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ku-&lt;del_in/&gt;iš&lt;del_fin/&gt;&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; and reads &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;ŠÀ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;É&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;DINGIR&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;-LIM&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-pát&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;kuiš&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;del_in/&gt; &lt;space c=&quot;8&quot;/&gt; &lt;del_fin/&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;x-pát&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ḫu-eš-wa-an-za&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; in obv. II 35-36. However, the fact that the enclitic particle &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-pát&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; is attached to the first word in obv. II 36 suggests that the latter is the beginning of a new sentence, which is used to exclude other possibilities of divine wrath (see &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;Hoffner H.A. − Melchert H.C. 2008a&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;, p. 387 §28.136). The relative clauses in obv. II 31and obv. II 35 thus both end in &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;kuiš.&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; The first clause in obv. II 36 is then likely to be read &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;&lt;del_in/&gt;a-pa-a-a&lt;del_fin/&gt;š-pát&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;TUKU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-u-wa-an-za.&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; For the shape of &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;TUKU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt; see the second sign in &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;TUKU.TUKU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;-&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;u-wa-an-za&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; in obv. II 37, for the use of &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-pát&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; in the conditional clause and &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;namma=ma&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; + negative word + indefinite pronoun in the main clause (&quot;if only ..., but not any other further/nothing else etc.) see, e.g., obv. II 23-24.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922528	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;For the restoration and the reading &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;TUKU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-u-wa-an-za&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; see the comment on obv. II 31.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922529	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Or &lt;laes_in/&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;TA&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;laes_fin/&gt;?&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922530	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;For this restoration see obv. II 14-15.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922531	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Restoration based on obv. I 6; obv. I 11 (both &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;pankuš=za&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;GÙB&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-tar&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;ḪUL&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-lu-ia&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;ME&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-aš&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;); obv. I 22 &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;(pankuš=za&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;GÙB&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-tar&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;ME&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-aš)&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;; obv. II 43 &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;(pankuš=za&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;GÙB&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-tar&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;GIG.GAL&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-ia&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;ME&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-aš)&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922532	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;In analogy to other passages maybe &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;URU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;ḪAT&lt;del_fin/&gt;-TI&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-ia&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; or &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;URU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;KÙ.BABBAR&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;-&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;TI&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-ia&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; (cf. obv. II 9, 14, 27). &lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922533	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Or &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;i-ia-u-e&lt;del_in/&gt;n.&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922534	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Or &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;URU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ka-a-t&lt;del_in/&gt;a-pa-ma&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; in analogy to rev. IV 13.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922535	Judging from the parallel passage in KUB 5.4+ rev. III 6, the space was probably left blank.
6922536	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;The restoration of this and the following lines is based on similar passages in the same text (see, e.g. obv. I 16 ff. and obv. I 26ff.).&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922537	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;According to the photo, the sign is written with an additional Winkelhaken and a second horizontal wedge. Probably the scribe initially wanted to write the sign &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;RU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt; and thus the 3. pers. pl. imperative &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;taruppantaru&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; as in obv. II 10 and obv. I 47. &lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922538	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Text: &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;PA&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt; instead of &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;RU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922539	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;End of this and the following lines restored from the analogous passages i 1ff.; 16ff. etc.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922540	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;In contrast to cuneiform copy by Walther in KUB 5.4, the vertical is completely visible on the photo.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922541	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;The broken end of the line was probably blank since attributes that accompany the word &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;MUŠEN&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;ḪI.A&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt; &quot;birds&quot;, such as &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ḫatuga/i-&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &quot;terrible, scary&quot; or &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;laḫlaḫ(ḫ)ima-&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &quot;concern, worry, agitation&quot;, usually precede it. For references see &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;HW2 III/1&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;, 526-527 s.v. &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ḫatuga/i-&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; and CHD L-N, p. 11-12 s.v. &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;laḫlaḫ(ḫ)ima-&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922542	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Text: &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;TI&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SIGN&gt;.&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
6922543	 &lt;P_f_Footnote&gt;Restoration based on obv. I 3 (partly broken); obv. I 18; obv. I 28; obv. II 9; rev. III 5. Alternatively, the less frequent spelling &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;me-ia-an-na-aš-ša-aš-ši&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; could be restored (cf. obv. I 39; obv. II 22).&lt;/P_f_Footnote&gt;
